<description>
Fill the black gaps by continuing the smallest rectangular periodic color tile.

Input structure
A grid contains a non-black rectangular periodic pattern with some black pixels
removed from it.

Rule
Find the unique smallest-area period rectangle whose residue classes are
consistent across all non-black pixels and all observed at least once, then
replace each black pixel by the color at the same row/column residue.

Key insight
The black pixels are missing samples from a repeating two-dimensional pattern,
not objects to preserve.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "non-black pixels of a periodic rectangular color pattern with black missing cells",
  "transform": "infer the unique smallest rectangular tile consistent with all non-black pixels; fill each black pixel with the tile color at the same row/column residue"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 22x22 (fixed)
  tile:
    shape: NxN square, N in 3-8
    symmetry: transpose (tile == tile.T) [observed]
    colors: 3-7 distinct non-black colors (no color 0 in tile)
    uniqueness: exactly one minimal-area tile consistent with all known pixels
  holes:
    count: 4-5 rectangular regions of black (color 0)
    sizes: 4-34 cells each; total 46-65 cells (9-14% of grid)
    shape: rectangular bbox, nearly always perfectly filled [observed]
    placement: scattered, non-adjacent (8-connected), may touch grid edges
  constraint: every tile cell (r%N, c%N) must have >=2 known observations
  output: fill all black cells with tile color at matching (row%N, col%N)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose tile size N from {3,4,5,6,7,8}
    2. Generate an NxN transpose-symmetric tile using 3-7 non-black colors (no 0); ensure tile has no smaller valid sub-period (check that no (pr,pc) with pr*pc < N*N yields a consistent tile)
    3. Tile the full 22x22 grid with the pattern (out[r][c] = tile[r%N][c%N])
    4. Place 4-5 non-overlapping, non-8-adjacent rectangular hole regions (2-6 rows x 2-7 cols each, total 46-65 cells); verify every tile cell still has >=2 remaining observations
    5. Set hole pixels to 0 to produce the input
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

